                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "<div>While we can cite many specific examples of drugs that do not meet this rule, oral drugs are <em>normally</em> best taken one hour before or two hours after a meal.</div>\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": false,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "If there is a high motility in the GIT, it will absorb drugs faster because everything is sped up\n"
                },
                {
                  "correct": true,
                  "tipsAndFeedback": {
                    "tip": "",
                    "chosenFeedback": "",
                    "notChosenFeedback": ""
                  },
                  "text": "Water soluble drugs normally need to move into the cells of the GIT through channels, from the area of higher concentration to the area of lower concentration. \n"
                }
